+## Carbon measurement & scheduling integration
+
+This document explains how the Aegis carbon metering and scheduling tools work and how to use them.
+
+Components
+- ops/carbon/co2_client.py — fetches CO2Signal current intensity & forecast.
+- ops/carbon/pue_config.yaml — per-region PUE values and procurement notes.
+- ops/carbon/job_energy_meter.py — wrapper to run jobs while sampling GPU power (nvidia-smi), compute kWh and kgCO2, write manifest and expose Prometheus metrics.
+- ops/carbon/job_scheduler.py — recommends the best start window in the next N hours based on forecast and PUE.
+- ops/carbon/job_wrapper.sh — convenience wrapper to pick best window, delay job, and run meter.
+- ops/monitoring/carbon_prometheus_exporter.py — aggregates job manifests and writes Prometheus textfile metrics.
+- services/policy/opa/carbon_policy.rego — simple OPA policy skeleton for region choice based on preference.
+- ops/ci/enforce_carbon_policy.sh — CI check to ensure new training jobs are instrumented.
+
+Quick start
+1. Configure:
+   - export CO2SIGNAL_API_KEY=<your-key>
+   - optional: export PUE_CONFIG_PATH=ops/carbon/pue_config.yaml
+   - optional: export PROM_TEXTFILE_DIR=/var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector
+2. Run a job via wrapper:
+   - ./ops/carbon/job_wrapper.sh "python3 services/models/multimodal/pytorch_lightning_recipe.py --processed-manifest ..." 240 carbon
+3. Aggregate metrics:
+   - Run ops/monitoring/carbon_prometheus_exporter.py periodically (cron) to expose aegis_total_co2_kg and aegis_total_energy_kwh to Prometheus.
+
+Notes
+- job_energy_meter prefers to use `nvidia-smi`. If it's not available, the script will still run but will produce an estimate of zero for sampled power — you should provide estimator or cloud metering integration for better accuracy.
+- For cloud metering integrate provider APIs to fetch actual host energy use where available and adapt job_energy_meter to use that.
+- Use job_scheduler to decide placement (region) or delay. Actual enforcement (submitting to Kubernetes at that time) must be implemented in your job submitter; job_wrapper.sh demonstrates one approach (sleep until window).
+
